From: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ufs-qcom: fix initialization and link startup on ACPI platforms

When booting via ACPI (e.g. device QCOM24A5), several issues prevent
the UFS controller from probing successfully:

1. Reset controller: host->rcdev.dev was not set under ACPI, causing
   a NULL pointer dereference in __dev_fwnode when devm_reset_controller_register()
   is called. Setting host->rcdev.dev = dev resolves the NULL dereference.

2. Interconnect: devm_of_icc_get() returns -ENODEV under ACPI because
   dev->of_node is NULL, causing ufs_qcom_icc_init() to fail and abort
   driver probing. Returning 0 when has_acpi_companion(dev) is true avoids
   failing the probe, while also ensuring err is cleanly set to 0.

3. Generic PHY: host->generic_phy is NULL under ACPI because the PHY
   is pre-initialized by firmware. However, ufs_qcom_power_up_sequence()
   blindly dereferenced phy->power_count, causing a NULL pointer crash at
   offset 0x344. Returning 0 under ACPI bypasses the PHY power-up sequence
   safely.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -493,6 +493,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_power_up_sequence(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	enum phy_mode mode;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (has_acpi_companion(hba->dev))
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * HW ver 5 can only support up to HS-G5 Rate-A due to HW limitations.
 	 * If the HS-G5 PHY gear is used, update host_params->hs_rate to Rate-A,
@@ -1514,6 +1517,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_icc_init(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 	struct device *dev = host->hba->dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (has_acpi_companion(dev))
+		return 0;
+
 	host->icc_ddr = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "ufs-ddr");
 	if (IS_ERR(host->icc_ddr))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(host->icc_ddr),
@@ -1572,6 +1578,7 @@ static int ufs_qcom_init(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	}
 
 	/* Fire up the reset controller. Failure here is non-fatal. */
+	host->rcdev.dev = dev;
 	host->rcdev.of_node = dev->of_node;
 	host->rcdev.ops = &ufs_qcom_reset_ops;
 	host->rcdev.owner = dev->driver->owner;
